title: Fix `eth_subscribe("newHeads")` in the ETH RPC
doc:
- audience: [Node Dev, Node Operator]
  description: |-
    `eth_subscribe("newHeads")` is now accepted. It was previously rejected
    with an invalid-params error because the server only accepted the
    non-standard `newBlockHeaders` name, which is no longer accepted.

    `newHeads` notifications now include `difficulty` and `mixHash`. Clients
    such as alloy require both fields to decode a block header.
crates:
- name: pallet-revive-eth-rpc
  bump: major
  validate: false
